  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Education and AI (Artificial Intelligence in Education, AIED) denotes the deployment of machine-learning systems\u2014intelligent tutoring systems (ITS) such as Carnegie Learning Mathia at 600K+ US students across 1,500+ districts, ALEKS at 25M+ cumulative users since 1996, Knewton (acquired Wiley 2019 for ~$17M after raising $157M), Squirrel AI at 5M+ K-12 Chinese students across 4,000+ centres in 700+ cities; conversational AI tutors built on large language models such as Khan Academy Khanmigo (GPT-4) at 1M+ students across 90+ districts free to US/Canada teachers from August 2024, Synthesis Tutor ($35M Series A 2024, Andreessen Horowitz) at $35/month family plan, Mathpresso QANDA at 90M+ users across 50+ countries, Brilliant.org at 10M+ active learners, MagicSchool AI at 4M+ educators across 6,000+ US schools with 80+ teacher tools at $99/teacher/year; generative-AI assistants (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini) used by 26% of US teens 13-17 for schoolwork per Pew Research 2024 (up from 13% in 2023) and 70% of teens for any generative AI per Common Sense Media 2024; AI grading and integrity tooling (Gradescope at 2,600+ universities processing 100M+ submissions reducing grading time 70%, Turni",
